1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,430
You made $500. Proud? Depends what you risked.

2
00:00:04,431 --> 00:00:07,999
Risked $100: +5R. Risked $2,000: +0.25R.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,999
R is what you lose if the stop hits.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,999
Entry $50, stop $48, 50 shares: 1R = $100.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,227
Now measure with it. $58 is +4R.

6
00:00:20,228 --> 00:00:23,999
Stopped out instead? −1R. Every time.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,723
20 trades, counted in R. Every loser: −1R.

8
00:00:27,724 --> 00:00:29,275
Total: +3.5R.

9
00:00:29,276 --> 00:00:33,723
$350 on a small account. $35,000 on a big one.

10
00:00:33,724 --> 00:00:35,999
R doesn't care which.

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,645
"Lost $300? Eh, one bad trade."
−3R? Your stop was more of a suggestion.

12
00:00:39,646 --> 00:00:43,999
Or the price gapped past it. Either way, find out.

13
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,965
Dollars say how much. R says how well.

14
00:00:48,966 --> 00:00:51,999
Same ruler, every trade.

15
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:57,949
Lore 003. Next: Lore 004, Legend 01: Jesse Livermore
